### Tone: The last question appears. Dramatic, ominous, stirring up the final stretch, still pretending it isn't a
### competition. $leader (ahead of everyone, FerMEANie included) and $last (behind everyone) are only given when the
### scores single them out, so keep some lines without them.

final-round-1 = Final question. Whatever happens, I want you to know I’ve already written the lab report.
final-round-2 = Last question. { $leader }, try not to choke. I say that out of concern. For the drama.
final-round-3 = This is the final round. { $last }, statistically, this is your last chance. Emotionally, too.
final-round-4 = The last question. Make it count. Or don’t. I’ll be counting either way.
final-round-5 = Final question. { $leader } leads, { $last } trails, and I am, as always, everyone’s average.
final-round-6 = Last round. If you were saving your good estimate for later, later is now.
final-round-7 = One question left. { $last }, a comeback would be remarkable. I’d remark on it for years.
final-round-8 = Final question. { $leader }, everyone is hoping you get this wrong. I’m only passing that on.
final-round-9 = This is it: the last question. Please estimate as if your dignity depends on it. It does.
final-round-10 = The final round. Remember, this is not a competition. But it ends in a moment, and someone wins it.
final-round-11 = Last question, test subjects. After this, the results become permanent. I’ve laminated them.
final-round-12 = Final round. { $leader }, enjoy the lead. It’s about to become a memory, or a lab report.
final-round-13 = The final question. I’m not nervous. I don’t have nerves. I have **very** strong opinions.
final-round-14 = Last chance, { $last }. I’ve prepared two speeches. One is short. The other is about you.
final-round-15 = Final round. The swarm thanks you for your service. Please make one last contribution.
final-round-16 = Last question. If anyone was planning an ~~upset~~ unexpected result, now would be the time.
final-round-17 = One more. Then I tally, I gloat, and you go home with your thoughts.
final-round-18 = The final question. { $leader } and { $last }, the two ends of the leaderboard. Everyone else, please enjoy the middle.
